    "description": "One 32-team bracket per classification, split into 4 regions of 8 qualifiers each. Designed for much larger regions where every good team gets a postseason game. Round 1 (Regional Quarterfinal): inside each region the top 8 play 1v8, 2v7, 3v6, 4v5. Round 2 (Regional Semifinal): the four regional QF winners play (1/8 winner vs 4/5 winner; 2/7 winner vs 3/6 winner). Round 3 (Regional Final): the two regional SF winners meet to crown a regional champion. Round 4 (Semifinal): the four regional champions are re-seeded by overall wins / point differential -- highest vs lowest, middle two vs each other. Round 5 (Championship): state title.",
